      <li><strong>Definition recall is the dominant cognitive demand.</strong> &ldquo;Define&rdquo; appears 60 times&mdash;more than any other action verb. This means the exam heavily rewards memorization of terminology, though &ldquo;write a program&rdquo; (54 occurrences) ensures application skills are also tested.</li>
      <li><strong>C programming and DBMS/MS Access are the two pillars.</strong> Every exam allocates roughly half its content to each domain. This dual focus has been consistent across the entire 11-year span.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Data Limitations</h3>
    <ul style="padding-left: 1.2rem; font-size: 0.92rem;">
